  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP FTMA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	Follow up on existing WFP-supported farmer savings groups and provide support where necessary to scale up savings and establish formal linkages with MFIs-Phase 1
2.	Establish and/or support existing savings groups in new WFP project sites-Phase 2
3.	As part of the phase 2 expansion, Establish/support new cooperatives with savings groups in new WFP project sites-Phase 3
4.	Build on the existing training material for savings group formation by strengthening existing modules and adding new modules relevant for additional stakeholders (including financial institutions / financial service providers, local authorities, cooperative leaders);  
5.	In partnership with interested financial institutions and private sector partners, develop, disseminate and evaluate specialized financial product(s) for WFP-supported groups that will enable savings groups members to leverage their savings for increased access to productive assets and equipment to grow their farming businesses;  
6.	Create and disseminate audio-visual knowledge management products to sensitize stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FTMA and ICCO have an ongoing collaboration since 2016 to link financial service providers to producer organizations for finance in the value chain. Agricultural cooperatives in Rwanda and in other African countries face a number of challenges including low productivity of members, limited access to markets for their products, lack of adequate management and limited access to finance. Access to a comprehensive range of financial services is a challenge for smallholder members in cooperatives. In April 2021 WFP and ICCO/Cordaid concluded a new collaboration for the period of 2 years.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maize, Beans, Horticulture Smallholder farmers in 75 cooperatives (Producer Organisation)
&#x2022;	25 cooperatives for the existing WFP-supported farmer savings groups 
&#x2022;	25 cooperatives for the existing savings groups in new WFP sites
&#x2022;	25 cooperatives for the new savings groups in new project sites</narrative>
  </description>
